 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: \"Rathe\" in the old spelling, \"geh'n\" and \"Wiederseh'n\" with the apostrophe, and the repeats of the music (the Ladies sing \"Sie werden eure Führer sein, folgt ihrem Rathe ganz allein\" twice; all five end with \"auf Wiederseh'n\" three times). Each Lady has her own line; in bars 24–31 the print puts all three on one staff. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
